// ============================================================================
// Things to look at in the capital (Chapter 3): one knot per interactable in
// src/data/areas/capital/*.ts. DRAFT text for the designer to rewrite: short,
// in the prince's eye, saying nothing nobody here would say.
// ============================================================================

// --- The citadel's halls ---

=== halls_statue ===
A ruler in marble, worn smooth at the toe where people touch it for luck.
Nobody remembers which one.
-> END

=== halls_screen ===
The great screen over the stair: the city, the weather, the day's audiences.
Your father's face, now and then, saying nothing much in a calm voice.
-> END

=== halls_portraits ===
The rulers before your father, one after another down the gallery.
Every one of them looks tired. The painters were kind about everything else.
-> END

=== halls_tube ===
A brass tube along the ceiling. A capsule shoots through it with a hiss and drops away into the diplomat's door.
Messages, all day, all night.
-> END

=== halls_lift ===
A glass lift between the floors, for those who can't be seen on the stairs.
You've always taken the stairs.
-> END

// --- Your quarters ---

=== quarters_bed ===
A bed with a canopy, bigger than some homes below. Made, unmade, made again by someone you never see do it.
-> END

=== quarters_mirror ===
You, in the coat. Wine at the collar, gold down the front.
You look like him. Everyone says so.
-> END

=== quarters_blades ===
Practice blades, nicked from years of lessons, and the dummy that never wins.
-> END

=== quarters_game ===
A game of rule, left mid-game. Your move. It's been your move for a week.
-> END

=== quarters_telescope ===
Your telescope, pointed at the horizon.
Far off, a tree, so big it shouldn't be. It's always been there. Nobody talks about it.
-> END

// --- The audience hall ---

=== audience_gate ===
The old castle's gate, stone older than anything else in the city. The portcullis is raised and rusted there for good.
They built the hall round it rather than take it down.
-> END

=== audience_benches ===
Benches for the people waiting to be heard. The wood is worn pale where they sit for hours.
-> END

=== audience_seat ===
Your seat, beside the throne and a step lower.
Close enough to see everything. Not close enough to decide anything.
-> END

=== audience_throne ===
The throne: tall, gold, uncomfortable. You've sat in it once, as a boy, when nobody was looking.
-> END

// --- The council chamber ---

=== council_table ===
The table of light: the whole city in blue, district by district, a scan sweeping it.
Some districts are dimmer than they used to be.
-> END

=== council_empty_seat ===
A councillor's seat, its light dark. Nobody's sat here in a while.
Nobody's said why.
-> END

=== council_top_seat ===
Your father's seat, at the top, where he can see every face.
-> END

// --- Your father's study ---

=== study_model ===
The city under glass: the citadel at the top, every street below it, every lift.
Small enough to hold in your arms.
-> END

=== study_books ===
Books, real ones, the only ones in the citadel. Laws, treaties, histories.
Some of the spines are worn white. Some have never been opened.
-> END

=== study_hearth ===
The castle's own hearth: the only real fire in the citadel. He keeps it lit.
-> END

=== study_clock ===
A case clock, older than the city's screens. It's never right. He never lets anyone fix it.
-> END

=== study_desk ===
His desk, papers squared to the edges. Nothing out of place.
A pen laid down mid-word.
-> END

// --- The sealed wing ---

=== sealed_statue ===
The last statue before the gold runs out. After it, nothing but bare walls.
-> END

=== sealed_cables ===
Cables along the ceiling and the floor, thick as your arm. Light runs through them, into the door.
They hum. You can feel it in your teeth.
-> END

=== sealed_door ===
A plain door. No handle on this side. Blue light at its edges.
Only your father goes through.
-> END

// --- The glasshouse ---

=== glasshouse_tree ===
A small tree in a gold pot. The only trees in the city are in this room.
-> END

=== glasshouse_trellis ===
Vines climbing a trellis towards the glass. Someone ties them up every morning.
-> END

=== glasshouse_fountain ===
The fountain: water, running, for nothing but the sound of it.
-> END

=== glasshouse_glass ===
The glass roof, beaded with water from the inside. The sky looks softer through it.
-> END

// --- The banquet gallery ---

=== banquet_mirrors ===
Mirrors in gold frames, all down the wall, so the room looks twice as full.
It needs to, lately.
-> END

=== banquet_table ===
The long table, laid for more people than come.
-> END

=== banquet_chair ===
Your father's chair, at the head of the table. Higher than the others.
-> END

=== banquet_balcony ===
The balcony, over the city. The lights go all the way down, and then they stop.
-> END

// --- The diplomat's office ---

=== office_notes ===
Notes pinned up in a hand you know. Names, places, times. Half of them crossed out.
-> END

=== office_maps ===
A wall of maps, pins and threads between them: the city, its districts, places beyond the wall you've never heard named.
-> END

=== office_desk ===
His desk: letters, seals, a capsule from the tube still warm.
Everything in piles that only make sense to him.
-> END

=== office_drawers ===
Brass drawers, each one labelled. All of them locked.
-> END

// --- The guest wing ---

=== guest_bed ===
Your friend's room: a bed, a wardrobe, a lamp. Everything a guest could want.
-> END

=== guest_door ===
A guest's door, shut. A name on a card beside it.
-> END

=== guest_window ===
A window behind a gold lattice. Pretty. It doesn't open.
-> END

=== guest_cages ===
Gilded birdcages hanging along the corridor. Empty. Their doors are shut anyway.
-> END

// --- The promenade ---

=== promenade_screen ===
The great screen on its mast: the news, notices, your father's face.
People look up at it the way they look at the weather.
-> END

=== promenade_signs ===
Signs of light over the shops, flickering where the power's weak.
-> END

=== promenade_view ===
From the walkway: the square below, the stalls steaming, and up above it all, the citadel. You can just see your balcony.
-> END

// --- The lifts ---

=== lifts_glass ===
Down through the glass: the city, falling away level by level, all the way to the street.
-> END

=== lifts_booth ===
The lift operator's old booth at the street. A stool, a cup, a screen of who went where.
-> END

// --- The low district ---

=== low_mark ===
Chalked on the wall: a wing over a bar of ground.
You've seen it before. You don't know where.
-> END

=== low_scrubbed ===
The same wing, half scrubbed off. Someone worked hard at it. Not hard enough.
-> END

=== low_homes ===
Homes stacked on homes, patched with whatever was to hand. Through a window, someone cooking for too many people.
-> END

=== low_washing ===
Washing strung between the cables, drip-drying over the street.
-> END

=== low_noodles ===
A noodle shop: a counter, steam, three stools. The smell follows you down the street.
-> END

// --- The hideout ---

=== hideout_emblem ===
The wing again, painted big on the old stone, over its bar of ground.
Down here nobody's scrubbing it off.
-> END

=== hideout_notices ===
Notices pasted over notices. The capital's orders, and over them, other people's.
-> END

=== hideout_back_way ===
A low door at the back, out into the dark. For when the front isn't safe.
-> END

// --- The data centre ---

=== data_racks ===
Racks in rows, blinking. Requests going out, output coming in.
Nobody says to where.
-> END

=== data_screens ===
The operator's screens: numbers moving faster than you can read them.
-> END

=== data_door ===
A sealed door, like the one in the citadel. The cables run into it here too.
-> END

// --- The gate ---

=== gate_wall ===
The city wall: old stone, dull gold, a passage through it barely wide enough for a cart.
-> END

=== gate_booth ===
The watch's booth: a screen of who's come in, and a shorter one of who's gone out.
-> END

=== gate_road ===
The road, going out across the waste. On the horizon, the tree.
-> END
